{{!-- Excel-only template (ETP-4899) — flattens the indented tree into a plain,
      calculation-friendly grid. The HTML preview conveys hierarchy with left
      padding, which Excel cannot express, so the tree indent becomes its own
      sortable "Depth" column plus separate code/name columns.
      "Depth" is the position in the report tree, NOT the account type: the
      same type can sit at different depths in different branches. The "Type"
      column (ETP-5663) is the account's ElementLevel (Heading / Account /
      Breakdown / Subaccount, contract `labels.E|C|D|S`), or "Total"
      (`labels.T`) for a formula HEADING (`isFormula` + level E: A.TOTAL,
      P.TOTAL, P.G.A..D). A formula at another level is a mirror account such
      as (5510) = -1 x 5510, not a total, so it keeps its own type. Built
      from the Handlebars built-ins `if`/`lookup` plus the canonical `ifCond`,
      so it needs no report-specific helper. Every header comes from
      `meta.labels`, with the same keys as template-csv.hbs.
      Amount cells use data-cell-type="number" with the RAW value (no
      formatCurrency) — html-to-xlsx does `parseFloat(cell.innerText)` for that
      type, so a formatted amount would silently truncate at the thousands
      separator. Never format here.
      Variation columns (ETP-6080): only with a comparison AND only for a
      contract that declares `labels.variationAmount` (Profit & Loss; the
      Balance Sheet shares this file byte for byte and has no variation yet).
      Raw values like the amounts, rounded to 2 decimals (round2); a null value (no % when the reference is 0)
      is an empty cell typed "string" via numCellType, never an empty number cell (html-to-xlsx writes NaN).
      Period columns (ETP-6239): with `meta.periods` the amount columns become one group per
      bucket (every bucket, the range total last), each `label`, and with a comparison also
      `label Compared (compared period)`, `label Var.` and `label Var. %`. The Balance Sheet copy of this file
      keeps the same loops, which come out empty for it (it never sends `periods`). --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><meta charset="UTF-8">
<style>
  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; }
  th { font-weight: bold; text-align: left; background: #f1f5f9; }
  th, td { padding: 1px 4px; white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <table>
    <thead><tr>
      <th>{{meta.labels.hdrGroup}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.hdrDepth}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.hdrType}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.hdrCode}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.hdrName}}</th>
      {{#if meta.periods}}
      {{#each (periodOrder meta.periods) as |idx|}}
      {{#with (periodLabel (lookup @root.meta.periods idx) @root.meta.params.columns @root.meta.locale @root.meta.labels.T) as |label|}}
      <th>{{label}}</th>{{#if (periodMode @root.meta.params.compareMode)}}<th>{{label}} {{periodComparedHeader @root.meta.labels.periodCompared @root.meta.params.periods idx @root.meta.params.compareMode @root.meta.params.columns @root.meta.locale}}</th><th>{{label}} {{@root.meta.labels.periodVarAmount}}</th><th>{{label}} {{@root.meta.labels.periodVarPct}}</th>{{/if}}
      {{/with}}
      {{/each}}
      {{else}}
      <th>{{meta.labels.amount}}</th>
      {{#ifCond meta.params.compareTo '===' 'true'}}<th>{{meta.labels.amount_ref}}</th>{{#if meta.labels.variationAmount}}<th>{{meta.labels.variationAmount}}</th><th>{{meta.labels.variationPct}}</th>{{/if}}{{/ifCond}}
      {{/if}}
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{#each rows}}
      <tr>
        <td>{{this.group}}</td>
        <td data-cell-type="number">{{this.indent}}</td>
        <td>{{#if this.isFormula}}{{#ifCond this.elementlevel '===' 'E'}}{{@root.meta.labels.T}}{{else}}{{lookup @root.meta.labels this.elementlevel}}{{/ifCond}}{{else}}{{lookup @root.meta.labels this.elementlevel}}{{/if}}</td>
        <td>{{this.value}}</td>
        <td>{{this.name}}</td>
        {{#if @root.meta.periods}}
        {{#each (periodOrder @root.meta.periods) as |idx|}}
        {{#with (lookup ../cells idx) as |cell|}}
        <td data-cell-type="number">{{cell.amount}}</td>{{#if (periodMode @root.meta.params.compareMode)}}{{#with (lookup cell (periodMode @root.meta.params.compareMode)) as |ref|}}<td data-cell-type="number">{{ref.amount}}</td><td data-cell-type="{{numCellType ref.variationAmount}}">{{round2 ref.variationAmount}}</td><td data-cell-type="{{numCellType ref.variationPct}}">{{round2 ref.variationPct}}</td>{{/with}}{{/if}}
        {{/with}}
        {{/each}}
        {{else}}
        <td data-cell-type="number">{{this.amount}}</td>
        {{#ifCond @root.meta.params.compareTo '===' 'true'}}<td data-cell-type="number">{{this.amount_ref}}</td>{{#if @root.meta.labels.variationAmount}}<td data-cell-type="{{numCellType this.variationAmount}}">{{round2 this.variationAmount}}</td><td data-cell-type="{{numCellType this.variationPct}}">{{round2 this.variationPct}}</td>{{/if}}{{/ifCond}}
        {{/if}}
      </tr>
      {{/each}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</body></html>
